# LOCAL run (2026-11-09; user chose "Random warm-up" after the plain-SAC fine-tune of
# c0 collapsed): slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac_plain.env with plain SAC's uniform-random
# start steps on the warm start (RANDOM_WARMUP=1): the first LEARNING_STARTS (20000)
# online transitions use uniform-random actions instead of c0's. Everything else as
# before: c0's demos pinned (arrival cut) and its 5000-update critic warm-up on them,
# then c0 drives with the actor frozen for 5000 critic-only updates, then the actor is
# released (~45k steps).
# Why: the previous run's critic saw only c0's narrow actions (expert |steer| ~0.03) and
# came out flat in the action -- any other steering or throttle moved Q by < 0.3% -- so
# the released actor chased a sign-flipping slope to full lock (steer lock 0.73 by 61k,
# goal success 0.16 by 158k).
. "$REPO/slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac_plain.env"
export RANDOM_WARMUP=1
